pve-meta-nvidia (0.0.2-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The per-node prefix document (nodes/<node>/prefixes/gpu, removed in
    pve-meta 0.2) becomes an entry in the cluster gpu file: inventory
    merges only nodes.<node>, bootstraps a missing file whole, and removes
    its entry when the driver is loaded with no cards. Needs pve-meta 0.2+.

 -- Julius Arkenberg <julius@rkenberg.de>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 21:30:00 +0200

pve-meta-nvidia (0.0.1-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First version. A container whose pve-meta document has a `gpu` subtree
    gets the node's GPUs through LXC's stock nvidia hook: cgroup device rules
    for the selected cards, the hook line, and the NVIDIA_* environment.
  * Each node writes its own cards into `nodes/<node>/prefixes/gpu`, so a
    guest is offered the GPUs of the node it is on and nothing else.
  * Verbs: daemon, inventory, reconcile, status.
  * The reconcile loop watches the documents of this node's containers and
    plans every one of them every poll; its first pass runs before
    pve-guests.service, because the nvidia-uvm major is allocated anew on every
    boot and that module is loaded lazily.
  * Every tool the loop runs has a deadline and is killed with its process
    group if it misses it, without waiting for the kill to work; the unit
    carries a systemd watchdog fed between bounded steps, so a wedged GPU tool
    cannot leave a daemon that runs and reconciles nothing.
  * The boot pass has a budget and takes no container config lock it cannot
    have at once, so being ordered before pve-guests.service never delays the
    containers by more than that.
  * Refuses a privileged container and a container with a `devN:` entry for an
    NVIDIA device, never touches a guest without a `gpu` key, and touches
    nothing at all on a node whose driver is not loaded.

 -- Julius Arkenberg <julius@rkenberg.de>  Thu, 17 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0200
